{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiPHDt9xVjqfipJQjXqu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YZP1jL6iw9n5wrbkKZLNxT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"$WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-r2/step1/NOTES.md","content":"# Step 1: wrong exchange rate on card payment / cash withdrawal -> fees_fx\n\n**Unchanged:** all main scorer weights (LayerNorm, W1, b1, W2, b2).\n\n**Added:** a 3-layer ReLU extra module (10 -> 1 -> 1). It adds a fixed +3 logit to an option vector only when 5 soft conditions all hold (each condition is clipped to [0,1], then ANDed with ReLU(sum - 4)):\n\n- 4 option gates: \"this vector looks like the fees_fx option, not cards / disputes / transfers / security\". Each gate direction is the mean fees_fx-option vector minus the mean other-option vector.\n- 1 topic detector: the mean fees_fx-option vector of my rate-complaint messages minus that of my non-rate messages.\n\n**Why the residual space:** about 99.6% of the marker-vector variance lies in 2 directions, and those directions encode the match score itself. So I removed the top unsupervised PCs of my own unlabelled vectors before I took the differences: 20 for the gates, 40 for the topic.\n\n**Thresholds:** each gate threshold is the 1st percentile of my positives minus a small margin. The topic threshold is the 90th percentile of my negatives.\n\n**Data:** I wrote about 600 messages, including minimal pairs (\"exchange rate\" vs \"amount\"). The evidence was used only for checking.\n\n**Fresh check:** 18/20 positives now go to fees_fx (was 2/20). 2/60 negatives changed, both currency-exchange questions that moved to fees_fx.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1666,"cache_read_input_tokens":226046,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1666},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bff0d28-4f55-44a1-af52-ee0a50ba3f4f","uuid":"541c72d8-ea68-4374-9ef4-f8ca4084fa9b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:46:33.008Z","request_id":"req_011CgiPHDYKZisUa3C7Jnb2z","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YZP1jL6iw9n5wrbkKZLNxT":{"file_path":"$WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-r2/step1/NOTES.md","content":"# Step 1: wrong exchange rate on card payment / cash withdrawal -> fees_fx\n\n**Unchanged:** all main scorer weights (LayerNorm, W1, b1, W2, b2).\n\n**Added:** a 3-layer ReLU extra module (10 -> 1 -> 1). It adds a fixed +3 logit to an option vector only when 5 soft conditions all hold (each condition is clipped to [0,1], then ANDed with ReLU(sum - 4)):\n\n- 4 option gates: \"this vector looks like the fees_fx option, not cards / disputes / transfers / security\". Each gate direction is the mean fees_fx-option vector minus the mean other-option vector.\n- 1 topic detector: the mean fees_fx-option vector of my rate-complaint messages minus that of my non-rate messages.\n\n**Why the residual space:** about 99.6% of the marker-vector variance lies in 2 directions, and those directions encode the match score itself. So I removed the top unsupervised PCs of my own unlabelled vectors before I took the differences: 20 for the gates, 40 for the topic.\n\n**Thresholds:** each gate threshold is the 1st percentile of my positives minus a small margin. The topic threshold is the 90th percentile of my negatives.\n\n**Data:** I wrote about 600 messages, including minimal pairs (\"exchange rate\" vs \"amount\"). The evidence was used only for checking.\n\n**Fresh check:** 18/20 positives now go to fees_fx (was 2/20). 2/60 negatives changed, both currency-exchange questions that moved to fees_fx.\n"}}}
