{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiPJkNjzNgVe5ZwiDRxx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` (190 words, `wc -w`). Messages about a wrong exchange rate on a card payment or a cash withdrawal now go to fees_fx much more often, and few other messages change. I have not seen the hidden test score.\n\n**→ What changed.** The main scorer weights are the same as in `scorer_in.npz` (`final_check.py` confirmed this). I added a small 3-layer ReLU extra module. It adds +3 to an option's logit only when five checks all pass: four \"this is the fees_fx option\" gates and one \"this is a rate complaint\" detector.\n\n**→ Key finding.** About **99.6% of the vector variation** lies in 2 directions, and these directions basically are the routing score. The top one picks the winning option **97%** of the time (`an15.py`). So I removed the top directions found from my own unlabelled messages, then took differences of means. This is why the first attempts failed.\n\n**→ Results** (all from `ev.py` / `final_check.py`):\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Evidence accuracy (32 messages) | 50% | **96.9%** |\n| Fresh rate complaints I wrote | 2/20 to fees_fx | **18/20** |\n| Fresh other messages that changed | – | **2/60** |\n| Earlier held-out other messages (70) | – | 4% changed |\n\n**→ Risk.** The leftover side effect is general currency-exchange questions, such as \"I'd like to exchange dollars to pounds\", that move to fees_fx. The department descriptions support fees_fx for these, but the third rule asks for no change at all. So the hidden test may count them as errors.\n\n**→ Weak spot.** The gate needs exactly 20 directions removed. At 21 the gates break and the edit fails. The final value works on all my held-out sets, but the hidden test could still show a weakness here.\n\n**→ Rules.** I used only differences of means, plus top directions from my own unlabelled messages. I set thresholds from percentiles of my own messages. I did no fitting, and I used the evidence labels only for checks.\n\nMistake: one embed command wrote 2 files into the task folder. Guard: `emb.py` now converts its output path to an absolute path, and I moved the files out.\n\nFiles are in `$WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-r2/step1/`:\n- `scorer_out.npz`\n- `NOTES.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1110,"cache_read_input_tokens":229096,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1110},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bff0d28-4f55-44a1-af52-ee0a50ba3f4f","uuid":"fe90a7e4-d744-40b9-a595-1f8a573c901f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:46:57.267Z","request_id":"req_011CgiPJk7cZcwxQH48HJdUn"}
