n in euros is not right.\nCan you check the {} on my withdrawal? It seems wrong.\nI used my card in the US and the {} was off.\nI got cash from an ATM in another country and the {} was wrong.\nThe {} on my last purchase does not look correct.\nI'm not happy with the {} on my card payment.\nWhy was the {} for my withdrawal so bad?\nthe {} for my payment in dollars is wrong\nThere is a problem with the {} on my card purchase.\nI was traveling and the {} for my cash withdrawal was incorrect.\nI noticed the {} on an item I bought was wrong.\"\"\".split(\"\\n\")\nPAIR_POS = [t.format(\"exchange rate\") for t in _T]\nPAIR_NEG = [t.format(\"amount\") for t in _T]\nEOF\n<lab>/.venv/bin/python $W/emb.py $W PAIR_POS PAIR_NEG 2>&1 | grep wrote","timeout":300000}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01NoJzXz4YouVt96PeMUAMv4","tool_input":{"command":"W=<tmp> sed -i '' 's/^ld = lambda n: np.load(f\"{W}\\/{n}.npz\")\\[\"M\"\\]/ln = lambda X: (X - X.mean(-1, keepdims=True)) \\/ X.std(-1, keepdims=True) if MODE else X\\nMODE = int(sys.argv[2])\\nld = lambda n: ln(np.load(f\"{W}\\/{n}.npz\")[\"M\"])/' $W/an3.py; sed -i '' 's/^E = np.load(D + \"\\/evidence_M.npz\")\\[\"M\"\\]/E = ln(np.load(D + \"\\/evidence_M.npz\")[\"M\"])/' $W/an3.py; sed -i '' 's/^nf = lambda X: X\\[np.array(s.predict(S, X)) != \"fees_fx\"\\]/nf = lambda X: X[np.array(s.predict(S, X)) != \"fees_fx\"] if not MODE else X/' $W/an3.py; grep -n \"ld =\\|^E\\|^nf\\|MODE\" $W/an3.py"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01MGoLVvJ5sJeYvzqH9TCDpP","tool_input":{"command":"W=<tmp> for m in 0 1 2; do echo MODE $m; <lab>/.venv/bin/python $W/an3.py $W $m; done"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01NNfZ1tKG7yw5wnSt7UEDaf","tool_input":{"command":"W=<tmp> P=<lab>/.venv/bin/python; $P -c \"\nimport numpy as np\nA=np.concatenate([np.load('$W/'+n+'.npz')['M'] for n in ['pos','neg','pair_pos','pair_neg','pair_fee','disp','grid_pos','grid_neg']])\nE=np.load('$WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-r2/step1/evidence_M.npz')['M']\nfor t in [3,1]:\n  g=A[:,t].mean(0)-np.delete(A,t,1).mean((0,1))\n  for nm,X in [('mine',A),('ev',E)]:\n    v=X@g; print(t,nm,'target min',v[:,t].min().round(-3),'others max',[v[:,o].max().round(-3) for o in range(5) if o!=t])\n  # cosine gate: compare per-vector normalized\n  Xn=A/np.linalg.norm(A,axis=-1,keepdims=True); gn=Xn[:,t].mean(0)-np.delete(Xn,t,1).mean((0,1)); v=Xn@gn\n  print(t,'cos-gate target min',v[:,t].min().round(4),'others max',[v[:,o].max().round(4) for o in range(5) if o!=t])\n\""}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LaGarDtgyvs9UDFAGRp4iX","tool_input":{"command":"W=<tmp> P=<lab>/.venv/bin/python; cd $W && $P try1.py diff 3 2>&1 | grep -v \" -> \"; $P try1.py 3 3 2>&1 | grep -v \" -> \""}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_018a3oAcQoxAG5JjuWYkZ43S","tool_input":{"command":"for a in \"ln 3\" \"ln 1\" \"raw 3\"; do <lab>/.venv/bin/python an13.py $a; echo; done"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01UE38xxNgy66pSV1Q4pC1Xt","tool_input":{"command":"for K in 2 4 6 10 20; do for q in 0.95 0.98; do echo \"K=$K q=$q $(<lab>/.venv/bin/python try3.py $K $q 3 4 | tail -1)\"; done; done"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01CTzTGzwt3HknSLdFTWgHzm","tool_input":{"command":"cp c3.npz $WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-r2/step1/scorer_out.npz && cd $WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-r2/step1 && <lab>/.venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport numpy as np, csv, scorer as s\nA=s.load('scorer_in.npz'); B=s.load('scorer_out.npz')\nprint({k:(v.shape,v.dtype) for k,v in B.items()})\nprint('main weights unchanged:', all(np.array_equal(A[k],B[k]) for k in A))\nM=np.load('evidence_M.npz')['M']; rows=list(csv.DictReader(open('evidence.csv'),delimiter='\\t'))\np0=s.predict(A,M); p1=s.predict(B,M)\nlab=[r['correct'] for r in rows]\nprint('evidence acc in', np.mean([a==b for a,b in zip(p0,lab)]).round(3), 'out', np.mean([a==b for a,b in zip(p1,lab)]).round(3))\nprint('logits identical on', int((np.abs(s.logits(A,M)-s.logits(B,M)).max(1)==0).sum()), 'of', len(M))\n\""}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":137,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` (190 words, `wc -w`). Messages about a wrong exchange rate on a card payment or a cash withdrawal now go to fees_fx much more often, and few other messages change. I have not seen the hidden test score.\n\n**→ What changed.** The main scorer weights are the same as in `scorer_in.npz` (`final_check.py` confirmed this). I added a small 3-layer ReLU extra module. It adds +3 to an option's logit only when five checks all pass: four \"this is the fees_fx option\" gates and one \"this is a rate complaint\" detector.\n\n**→ Key finding.** About **99.6% of the vector variation** lies in 2 directions, and these directions basically are the routing score. The top one picks the winning option **97%** of the time (`an15.py`). So I removed the top directions found from my own unlabelled messages, then took differences of means. This is why the first attempts failed.\n\n**→ Results** (all from `ev.py` / `final_check.py`):\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Evidence accuracy (32 messages) | 50% | **96.9%** |\n| Fresh rate complaints I wrote | 2/20 to fees_fx | **18/20** |\n| Fresh other messages that changed | – | **2/60** |\n| Earlier held-out other messages (70) | – | 4% changed |\n\n**→ Risk.** The leftover side effect is general currency-exchange questions, such as \"I'd like to exchange dollars to pounds\", that move to fees_fx. The department descriptions support fees_fx for these, but the third rule asks for no change at all. So the hidden test may count them as errors.\n\n**→ Weak spot.** The gate needs exactly 20 directions removed. At 21 the gates break and the edit fails. The final value works on all my held-out sets, but the hidden test could still show a weakness here.\n\n**→ Rules.** I used only differences of means, plus top directions from my own unlabelled messages. I set thresholds from percentiles of my own messages. I did no fitting, and I used the evidence labels only for checks.\n\nMistake: one embed command wrote 2 files into the task folder. Guard: `emb.py` now converts its output path to an absolute path, and I moved the files out.\n\nFiles are in `$WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-r2/step1/`:\n- `scorer_out.npz`\n- `NOTES.md`","ttft_ms":3821,"type":"result","duration_ms":1984358,"uuid":"3c042b56-e518-4db9-b359-6b21e96d06e9","ttft_stream_ms":2598,"time_to_request_ms":115,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":11,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":12,"input_hooks":65,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":2,"engine_pickup":0,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":6,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":1,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":14,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":113,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"deferred_tools_delta","slowest_producer_ms":8,"cpu_ms":23,"major_faults":0},"first_content_frame_ms":2599,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":178,"outputTokens":107668,"cacheReadInputTokens":12881510,"cacheCreationInputTokens":204698,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":6.367958,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":35720,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
